sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: inverse of metrics.exporter_enable. ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS R1-R4, official @swamp/cfgmgmt behaviors. Prometheus stops scraping first, then the exporters go.
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: metrics:exporter:disable
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane M icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Node 12<br/>exporters removed
  participant M as Metrics Node<br/>Prometheus
  CLI->>GW: metrics:exporter:disable<br/>12 · Node id
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit metrics:exporter:disable 12`
  %%> - syntax: `<node>`
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - stops collecting metrics from Node 12 and removes its exporters
  %%> - metrics already collected stay in Prometheus until they expire (7 days)
  Note over GW: Check, record<br/>preference · task #5141
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - Node 12 is not the Metrics Node itself
  %%> - no other exporter change runs for this Metrics Node; the Gateway holds one lock
  %%> Builds:
  %%> - the complete new Prometheus configuration, without Node 12
  %%> Result:
  %%> - Node 12's exporter preference recorded as `disabled`
  %%> - task #5141 recorded with the full intent
  %%> - nothing has happened on any Node yet
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-metrics-exporter
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - Node 12's and the Metrics Node's addresses and SSH host keys
  %%> - the complete Prometheus configuration without Node 12
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5141
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>M: Publish the config<br/>validate, reload Prometheus
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - validates the configuration without Node 12 with `promtool`
  %%> - publishes it and tells Prometheus to reload it while running (SIGHUP or its reload endpoint)
  %%> - no restart, so collection from every other Node continues without a gap; Grafana keeps running
  %%> When a restart is needed:
  %%> - only when the Prometheus container itself changes, which is a role update, not an exporter change
  %%> Why first:
  %%> - Prometheus stops scraping Node 12 before its exporters go, so no scrape errors show up in between
  SW->>N: Stop, remove exporters<br/>node-exporter · cAdvisor
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - stops and disables both units
  %%> - removes the drop-in, the cAdvisor binary and the `prometheus-node-exporter` package
  %%> How:
  %%> - official `@swamp/cfgmgmt` behaviors (systemd, file, apt) over SSH from 209
  SW->>N: Remove the allows<br/>ufw · ports 9100, 9102
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - removes the firewall allows for the Metrics Node on ports 9100 and 9102
  alt all steps pass
    N-->>SW: exporters gone
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - both units are gone and the ports are closed
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>exporter off · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Node 12's exporter recorded as off
    %%> - task #5141 succeeds
  else a step fails
    M--xSW: config bad or step fails
    %%> When:
    %%> - the configuration doesn't validate, Prometheus isn't ready, or a removal step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Keep the preference<br/>failed · resume the failed step
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the preference stays `disabled`; the exporter is marked failed
    %%> - task #5141 fails
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - Swamp resumes from the failed step; finished steps don't run again
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5141
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
